  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening The Measuring and Monitoring of SDG 16 In Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support the implementation of the SDG16 Survey, an international survey instrument jointly developed by UNDP, UNODC and OHCHR in collaboration with member states, that countries can use to measure progress on many of the survey-based indicators under SDG16. The initiative will support Sri Lanka to implement specific survey modules based on national needs and priorities which can be attached to household surveys primarily conducted by Department of Censors and Statistics (DCS).Th</narrative>
  </description>
